[
    {
        "id": "b1a2c3d4e5f60001",
        "type": "tab",
        "label": "S2 - Boiler (OMBC) demo",
        "disabled": false,
        "info": "Simulates a single-phase electric boiler as an S2 Resource Manager using Operation Mode Based Control (OMBC), without any real hardware.\n\nThe boiler has two operation modes: 'Standby/off operation' (0W) and 'Normal operation' (2500W on L2), configured on the 's2-ombc-config' node. s2-rm handles the generic S2 protocol; the 's2-ombc' node owns OMBC-specific behavior: it pushes the system description once the CEM selects OMBC, resolves OMBC.Instruction messages (emitting the mode's diagnostic_label as msg.topic), and reports OMBC.Status back to the CEM only once told the mode is confirmed - here simulated instantly by the 'Confirm mode achieved' node, standing in for real hardware feedback.\n\nA switch node on msg.topic records which mode is active in flow context; a separate 5s inject reads that back to build and send a PowerMeasurement reflecting the current mode.\n\nBefore deploying: open the 's2-cem-config' node and fill in the WebSocket URL (and credentials, if required) of the CEM you want to connect to.",
        "env": []
    },
    {
        "id": "b1a2c3d4e5f60002",
        "type": "comment",
        "z": "b1a2c3d4e5f60001",
        "name": "Setup",
        "info": "1. Open 's2-cem-config' and set the CEM WebSocket URL (+ credentials).\n2. Deploy.\n3. Once the CEM connects and selects OPERATION_MODE_BASED_CONTROL, s2-ombc pushes its system description and this flow simulates a boiler that reacts to OMBC instructions, confirms them instantly, and reports its (fake) power draw back every 5s.",
        "x": 200,
        "y": 60,
        "wires": []
    },
